  "id": "ovulatory-cycle",
  "term": "ovulatory cycle",
  "definition": "The ovulatory cycle is the recurring menstrual cycle that includes a fertile phase around ovulation. In the source, it is described as a cycle during which some features, such as facial skin redness, can vary across days, with redness rising before ovulation and staying relatively high through the luteal phase.",
